WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.910
Hattie McDaniel got one that was kind of given to her.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.200
I sincerely hope I shall always be a credit to my race.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.160
and to the motion picture industry.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.800
My heart is too full to tell you just how I feel.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.630
And I say thank you and God bless.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:22.870
Yes, she won that. I mean, and that's the you know, that's another conversation...

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:28.930
Of, you know, people talk about, well, why are you, why are you a proponent of Gone with the Wind?

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.200
She won an Oscar! She won an Oscar and broke everybody's face.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.410
They put her in the corner. They put baby in a corner.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.100
Is that we're calling a Patrick Swayze call back? Thank you.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.620
See, I'm keeping up. I'm trying to keep up with you.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.520
And the Oscar goes to... Whoopi Goldberg.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.820
That moment of going on stage, walking up those steps,

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.300
What was that like? What's going through your head?

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:02.190
Walking down an aisle to go up those steps?

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.890
I thought, OK, finally.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.790
Finally. I wanted this. I wanted it. You know?

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.630
And people said, "Well, you know, it's a comedy it's probably not going to work."

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.190
And I thought about all the, all the people, who didn't get it.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.630
And I thought, well...

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:28.940
I got it. I got this. This is mine, and that is also forever.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:34.440
That's part of my moniker, Academy Award Winner. Yup!

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.780
You know, I like that.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:44.280
Ever since I was a little kid, I wanted this.You don't know.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:50.640
My brother sitting there he's saying "Thank God we don't have to listen anymore. You can do it now."

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.840
My mom saw me. Everybody's watching.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:57.630
What's more fun, watching the Oscars at home or being there on the floor? On the stage?

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:03.630
Oh, well, now that I'm an old broad certainly being there is more fun.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.710
My daughter and I went a couple of years ago.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.640
Because I think I was presenting something, I don't know why I was there.

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:18.300
Oh, I do know. It was because Chris Rock was doing... He was hosting.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.230
Which time was it? Was it when he went to the Magic Johnson Theater?

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.780
Which is maybe one of the greatest moments in Oscars history.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.850
So I left the Kodak Theater and went down to the Magic Johnson Theater.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:32.460
Did you see Million Dollar Baby? No, I sure did. And I can't lie.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.130
And I'm not going in front of these people out here and tell you he has seen it.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.290
And he is just like, listen, you've got to put us in some shit.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.690
You I have to do everything, but now you've got to do it.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.340
Because now people calling you out about it.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:50.700
Then I counted at least 15 black people on that montage.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.810
And he's gone through, I think, to where people say things about the show.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.330
And then a few years later, go, "Oh, he was really good at it."

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.140
Is that part of the the thing that comes with it?

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.870
That people can't recognize what is you're doing.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.380
When you're hosting the Oscars that night because of the expectations?

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.520
That people.. In that way you're talking about?

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.760
People need distance to sort of judge you as an Oscars host?

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:16.980
I think so. I think so. You know, and they're judging.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:22.510
What you're doing without really sort of paying attention to what you're doing.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.570
It's like the, you know, coming out as Elizabeth.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:31.150
Good evening, loyal subjects. I am the African Queen.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:36.880
It felt like there were 500 thousand Elizabeth Movies.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.570
And Bette Davis did the greatest.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:44.350
I mean, I'm sorry, she did the greatest Elizabeth movie ever.

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:46.030
Elizabeth and Essex.Yeah, yeah.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.650
Yeah. That's what I patterned that visual on.

